[[File:Nagasakibomb.jpg|thumb|A mushroom cloud characteristic of an atomic bomb detonation.]]

===Etymology===
Coined by British science fiction author [[wikipedia:H. G. Wells|H. G. Wells]] in his 1914 novel ''[[wikipedia:The World Set Free|The World Set Free]]''.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A [[nuclear weapon]] that obtains its [[destructive]] [[energy]] from [[nuclear fission]].
#* {{quote-book
|en
|year=1914
|first=Herbert George
|last=Wells
|authorlink=H. G. Wells
|title=The World Set Free
|passage=The gaunt face hardened to grimness, and with both hands the bomb-thrower lifted the big '''atomic bomb''' from the box and steadied it against the side.
}}
#: {{syn|en|atom bomb|A-bomb|fission bomb}}

